// Ch3 Cutscene B, "The First Verse". Beats B09-B11 in docs/kb/story/beats/vertical_slice.md.
// Three nodes: Asha enters Ilun's chamber alone (S07, S08); Rhen and Toma wait on the steps (S06);
// sunset, Asha comes out and sings the first verse toward home (S09, S10); the Drownbell tolls (C08).
// Facial beats: Asha's exhausted joy; Rhen's recognition (S10 from the second sung line, held at
// least 6 s with no cutaway: surprised, then grief, layered with two @face cues).
// Camera grammar (decisions_log N-13): S07/S08 and S09/S10 are unrelated setups, so they cut.
// The verse is a Velamir family lullaby (decisions_log N-11): the women of the line hum it to their
// children. Imra hummed it as a girl; Dace heard it from her at Haluna before Rhen was born, never
// knowing her name, and met her only on the Corrow stair (ADR 0022). She hummed it to Asha nightly,
// sang it from this door when Asha was seven, and Asha forgot it until Ilun gave it back.
// Light rules (docs/kb/art/README.md): Ilun in his chamber is BOUND light (glimmer_bound: steady,
// never drifting). The light that comes off Asha's skin at sunset is RELEASED (glimmer_lift: warm
// gold, slow upward spirals). It is the first released light in the game. The Drownbell's wounds
// are HELD (glimmer_held: cyan, sinking). Nobody names the rule aloud.
// Lamptongue lines (#lamptongue) are not translated. #sung lines are carried by the music cue.
title: ch03_the_first_verse
location: ch03/shell_shrine
grade: ch03_shrine_int
---
@letterbox on
@camera S07
@music shell_shrine_interior fade=2.0
@anim asha walk_to_chamber
Asha [soft_smile]: Don't look so worried, both of you. It's only my first one. #line:ch03_verse_001
// M3-CIN-1236 (PC GPU QA row 60): S07 sat between Rhen's shoulder and Toma's shield; it is pulled back to a clear
// over-the-shoulder on Asha, and the two who stay answer her on S07R, the reverse from inside the hall.
@camera S07R
Rhen [worried]: Shout if it bites. #line:ch03_verse_002
@camera S07
Asha [laugh]: He's been in there a hundred and forty years. I think he'll be polite. #line:ch03_verse_003
@camera S07R
Toma [neutral]: We will be here, Lady Cantor. #line:ch03_verse_004
@camera S07
Asha [smile]: Toma. #line:ch03_verse_005
@camera S07R
Toma [tender]: ...Asha. #line:ch03_verse_006
@mark asha chamber_pool walk
// M2-FP-119: she is seen going in, a few steps into the hall, before the black (the fade had cut her at her first step).
@wait 1.4
@fade out 0.8
@anim asha idle_shift
@camera S08 blend=0.0
@fade in 0.8
@vfx glimmer_bound at=ilun_chamber form=ilun
@wait 2.5
@fade out 1.2
@music silence fade=1.2
<<jump steps>>
===
title: steps
location: ch03/shell_shrine
grade: ch03_steps
---
@camera S06
// M2-FP-119: seated under the black. After the fade, Rhen's 2.3 m stand-in glide to his tread showed as a slide.
@anim rhen sit_steps
@anim toma sit_steps
@fade in 1.0
@wait 1.5
Rhen [neutral]: So. How long does a verse take? #line:ch03_verse_007
Toma [neutral]: As long as it takes. The last time, the village waited on the beach until dark. #line:ch03_verse_008
Rhen [smile]: You weren't here for that one? #line:ch03_verse_009
// ADR 0022 (d): Toma was at Ansedra's temples in 1001 and came home only at Asha's naming (1009).
Toma [neutral]: I was at Ansedra then, at the temples. I heard of it by letter. #line:ch03_verse_061
@wait 1.5
Rhen [smile]: Do you ever put that spear down? #line:ch03_verse_011
Toma [soft_smile]: To eat. #line:ch03_verse_012
@wait 1.0
@anim toma look_at rhen
Toma [neutral]: Do you know what a Cantor is? #line:ch03_verse_013
Rhen [neutral]: ...Someone who sings? #line:ch03_verse_014
@wait 1.2
@face toma sad 1.0
Toma [sad]: Yes. Someone who sings. #line:ch03_verse_015
-> And then she comes home? #line:ch03_verse_016
    <<set $ch03_rhen_asked_after = true>>
    @wait 1.5
    Toma [sad]: Then the storm sleeps. For years. Children grow up who have never seen it. #line:ch03_verse_017
    Rhen [worried]: That's not an answer. #line:ch03_verse_018
    Toma [guilty]: No. It is not. #line:ch03_verse_019
-> Seems like a lot of fuss for one song. #line:ch03_verse_020
    @face toma determined 0.4
    Toma [determined]: You do not mock the rites, Rhen. You may ask about them. That is different. #line:ch03_verse_021
    Rhen [guilty]: I'm asking. Badly, but I'm asking. #line:ch03_verse_022
Toma [neutral]: Then ask her. Not me. She has earned the telling of it. #line:ch03_verse_023
@wait 1.0
// ADR 0022 (d): sworn at her naming, three years ago. Before that he was the Haluna boy home on leave.
Toma [soft_smile]: I have guarded her three years. Before that, on leave, I had to find her in the net racks. She hid on purpose. #line:ch03_verse_062
Rhen [smile]: And now? #line:ch03_verse_025
Toma [tender]: Now she does not hide. I find I miss it. #line:ch03_verse_026
<<if $ch02_rhen_stayed_with_dead>>
    @wait 1.0
    Toma [neutral]: This morning, in the water. You stayed with them. #line:ch03_verse_027
    Rhen [sad]: Somebody should have. #line:ch03_verse_028
    Toma [sad]: Yes. I think so too. #line:ch03_verse_029
<<endif>>
@fade out 1.5
// In the black, two hours on: they are on their feet when she comes out (S10 is the reverse on Rhen, facing her).
@mark rhen rhen_rise walk
@mark toma toma_rise walk
@wait arrive=rhen
@wait arrive=toma
<<jump threshold>>
===
title: threshold
location: ch03/shell_shrine
grade: ch03
---
@camera S09
// ADR 0017 watch: she walks out on her own feet. No stumble, no catch at the door, and no summon
// shown here. Ilun is first called in the Drownbell fight.
// M2-FP-119: the emerge starts under the black, so the fade finds her stepping out (S09 had faded in on an empty
// doorway, and then she popped into it from the inner pool).
@anim asha emerge_doorway
@fade in 2.0
<<set $ch03_ilun_bound = true>>
@anim rhen look_at asha
@anim toma look_at asha
@vfx glimmer_lift at=asha motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@face asha exhausted 1.0
Asha [exhausted]: Oh. It's evening. #line:ch03_verse_030
@camera S10 blend=0.0
Rhen [surprised]: You're glowing. Is that normal? Toma, is that normal? #line:ch03_verse_031
Toma [tender]: It is normal. #line:ch03_verse_032
@camera S09 blend=0.0
Asha [laugh]: It tickles. #line:ch03_verse_033
<<if $ch02_heard_pila>>
    Rhen [worried]: Was it him? The boy from the shells. Teyo. #line:ch03_verse_034
    Asha [sad]: He's still frightened. He was kind to me anyway. #line:ch03_verse_035
<<else>>
    Asha [tender]: He was kind to me. I didn't expect that. #line:ch03_verse_036
<<endif>>
<<if $ch03_found_net_float>>
    @anim rhen offer_item net_float
    Rhen [neutral]: Found this in the side pool. Seemed like it belonged to someone. #line:ch03_verse_037
    @face asha surprised 0.4
    Asha [surprised]: He carries one just like it. #line:ch03_verse_038
    @face asha soft_smile 1.0
    Asha [soft_smile]: Keep it. I think he'd like it to stay with someone who goes home. #line:ch03_verse_039
<<endif>>
Toma [neutral]: The verse. It is sung toward home first. #line:ch03_verse_040
Asha [soft_smile]: I know, Toma. I watched it once. #line:ch03_verse_041
@mark asha threshold_west walk
@anim asha face_west
// The four sung lines are hush_first_verse's four phrases (assets_src/music/hush_first_verse.py: the drone's
// 4 s in, then about 6.5 s a line with a 0.7 s breath; the piano enters on *mir* at 27.7 s). Each is #timed: it
// shows as its phrase starts and the @waits hold it, so the words land with the song, not with a button.
@music hush_first_verse fade=0.5
@wait 4.0
Asha [tender]: Vey ennu, vey ennu, #line:ch03_verse_042 #sung #timed #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue, the old Iskarran liturgical language (constructed). Keep exactly as written: the translation is never shown."
@wait 7.19
// S10 recognition: cut on the second phrase (he knows it from the first), Asha's voice over his
// face. Hold >= 6 s of waits on S10 (test_dialogue_vs_scenes.gd checks it). Surprise is brief and
// light; grief settles under it as he understands whose song it is.
@camera S10 blend=0.0
@face rhen surprised 0.3
Asha [tender]: hal oan, ish karra. #line:ch03_verse_043 #sung #timed #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue, the old Iskarran liturgical language (constructed). Keep exactly as written: the translation is never shown."
@wait 7.2
@face rhen grief 0.6
Asha [tender]: Ennu re, ennu re... #line:ch03_verse_044 #sung #timed #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue, the old Iskarran liturgical language (constructed). Keep exactly as written: the translation is never shown."
@wait 7.19
Asha [tender]: ...mir. #line:ch03_verse_045 #sung #timed #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue, the old Iskarran liturgical language (constructed). Keep exactly as written: the translation is never shown."
@wait 7.0
Rhen [grief]: ...where did you learn that? #line:ch03_verse_046
@camera S09 blend=0.0
Asha [surprised]: Just now. It's the first verse. #line:ch03_verse_047
@face asha worried 0.6
Asha [worried]: Rhen? #line:ch03_verse_048
-> My father hummed that. Every night. #line:ch03_verse_049
    <<set $ch03_rhen_named_lullaby = true>>
    Rhen [grief]: Every night until he didn't. #line:ch03_verse_050
    // Lead verdict (review-sweep-G B3, ADR 0022 append note): Act I never voices Asha's link between
    // the lantern and Rhen's father (lines 051/052 are cut). It surfaces only in Kerrid's Ch15
    // confession. The held beat below is the same on every path and says nothing about the lantern.
    @face asha neutral 0.4
    @wait 0.8
    Asha [tender]: My mother hummed it to me every night, and sang it from this door. I was seven. I'd forgotten it until tonight. #line:ch03_verse_063
    @wait 1.5
    Rhen [sad]: ...He never said where he learned it. #line:ch03_verse_054
-> Nowhere. Must have been the wind. #line:ch03_verse_055
    <<if $ch02_rhen_named_lantern>>
        Asha [soft_smile]: All right. Not today. #line:ch03_verse_056
    <<else>>
        Asha [soft_smile]: That's twice you haven't answered me, Rhen Sallow. I'm patient. #line:ch03_verse_057
    <<endif>>
<<set $ch03_first_verse_sung = true>>
@music silence fade=0.3
@sfx drownbell_toll at=causeway
@wait 1.5
@anim toma turn_seaward
Toma [determined]: The tide has turned. #line:ch03_verse_058
Asha [worried]: Something heard that. #line:ch03_verse_059
@mark asha drownbell_arena run
@mark toma drownbell_arena run
@mark rhen drownbell_arena run
@camera C08 blend=0.0 grade=ch03_boss
@sfx drownbell_toll at=drownbell
@vfx glimmer_held at=drownbell drift=down_seaward
Toma [determined]: On my shield. Everyone, on my shield, now. #line:ch03_verse_060
@letterbox off
<<event start_battle drownbell>>
===
